From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saifuddin Hitawala <hitawala@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:34:47 -0800
Subject: [gpu] Check GrContext flush success instead of semaphores

GrDirectContext flush returns a FlushResult that separates success
from GrSemaphoresSubmitted now, which was not happening earlier.
This change updates callsites to check for fSuccess properly instead
of implicitly checking the semaphore result.

Bug: 568937157
Cq-Exclude-Trybots: luci.chromium.try:dawn-win10-x86-deps-rel
Change-Id: I4179ac2e83f190e865caa781a66e91889d57e740
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8738496
Commit-Queue: Saifuddin Hitawala <hitawala@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kyle Charbonneau <kylechar@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1739361}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): the conflicting hunks only differed in
context: this branch spells the parameter type VulkanContextProvider* (not
gpu::VulkanContextProvider*) in the SkiaOutputDevice Flush() signatures, and
SharedContextState::SubmitIfNecessary keeps its base::debug::DumpWithoutCrashing()
call inside the now fSuccess-based failure branch. The return-type change to
bool and all .fSuccess checks apply as upstream.

